# Isolated task agents

This repo runs **one agent per task**. Tasks live in `tasks/<id>/`. Each task owns exclusive `allowed_paths`.

## Orchestrator (main checkout)

If `MDS_TASK_ID` is not set, you are the orchestrator.

- When the user adds work, create a new task with `./scripts/mds-task add <id> --title '...' --path 'exclusive/path' --body '...'`.
- That command assigns a dedicated agent, branch `task/<id>`, and worktree `.worktrees/<id>/`.
- Launch a worker only inside that worktree. Do not implement WordPress, theme, plugin, or page work in the main checkout.
- Never edit one task’s files while servicing another.
- Overlapping `allowed_paths` are forbidden. If two tasks need the same file, stop and split ownership.

## Worker

If `MDS_TASK_ID` is set, you are that worker.

- Edit only `tasks/<id>/` plus that task’s `allowed_paths`.
- Do not edit other task folders, `.cursor/`, `scripts/`, or `.git/`.
- Do not copy other agents’ plans. Do not expand scope.

## Add / remove

- Add: `./scripts/mds-task add <id> --title '...' --path 'file-or-glob'`
- Remove: `./scripts/mds-task remove <id>` — deletes only that task folder, branch, and worktree.
- Removing or reassigning one task must not change other task folders, branches, or worktrees.
